<main><section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="index.html">HOME</a> / KEY PERSONS</div><div class="eyebrow light"><span></span> TEAM TEXOL</div><h1>People behind the process</h1><p>Meet the experienced technical, engineering, business-development and finance professionals supporting TEXOL’s work.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="notice" style="margin-bottom:22px">TEXOL’s leadership brings together experience in chemical and mechanical engineering, industrial design, business development and finance.</div><div class="bio-grid"><article class="bio-card"><div class="bio-head"><div class="bio-monogram" aria-hidden="true">MP</div><div><h2>Mr. Mangesh Pitambare</h2><div class="role">Vice President – Technical</div><a href="mailto:mangesh@texol.in" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--navy)">mangesh@texol.in</a></div></div><p><strong>Education</strong><br>Master’s in Chemical Engineering (1987) and Bachelor’s in Chemical Engineering (1985), Mumbai University (UDCT).</p><p><strong>Professional experience</strong><br>Experience in design and execution of laboratory, pilot and mini chemical plants for research, process innovation and technology demonstration. His work spans process engineering from concept/design of experiments through commissioning and handover, including domestic and overseas consultancy and troubleshooting.</p></article><article class="bio-card"><div class="bio-head"><div class="bio-monogram" aria-hidden="true">VK</div><div><h2>Mr. Vijay Kumar K. P.</h2><div class="role">Director – Engineering Construction</div><a href="mailto:vijay@texol.in" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--navy)">vijay@texol.in</a></div></div><p><strong>Education</strong><br>B.E. Mechanical Engineering (1985), Regional Engineering College, Madras University; M.Des (1987), IIT Bombay.</p><p><strong>Professional experience</strong><br>Mechanical engineer and industrial designer with experience in chemical pilot plants, laboratory-scale plants, pilot-plant design, components and maintenance. TEXOL notes assignments involving China, Kuwait, Mexico, South Korea, Malaysia and Italy.</p></article><article class="bio-card"><div class="bio-head"><div class="bio-monogram" aria-hidden="true">AP</div><div><h2>Dr. Ashutosh Pande</h2><div class="role">Director – Business Development</div><a href="mailto:ashutosh@texol.in" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--navy)">ashutosh@texol.in</a></div></div><p><strong>Education</strong><br>Bachelor’s and Master’s in Chemical Engineering, Laxminarayan Institute of Technology, Nagpur; Ph.D. in Chemical Engineering, IIT Bombay.</p><p><strong>Professional experience</strong><br>TEXOL describes more than 22 years of experience in process engineering, techno-commercial proposals, business development, client relationships, international sourcing and project coordination.</p></article><article class="bio-card"><div class="bio-head"><div class="bio-monogram" aria-hidden="true">MK</div><div><h2>Mr. Madhav Kane</h2><div class="role">Director – Finance</div><a href="mailto:madhav.kane@texol.in" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--navy)">madhav.kane@texol.in</a></div></div><p><strong>Education</strong><br>M.Com. (1982) and LL.B. (1991), Pune University.</p><p><strong>Professional experience</strong><br>TEXOL describes more than 30 years across finance, legal, labour, HR, administration and IT, including company amalgamations, mergers, unit closures and ERP implementations.</p></article><article class="bio-card"><div class="bio-head"><div class="bio-monogram" aria-hidden="true">SJ</div><div><h2>Mr. Subodh Jejurkar</h2><div class="role">Assistant Vice President – Technical</div><a href="mailto:subodh@texol.in" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--navy)">subodh@texol.in</a></div></div><p><strong>Education</strong><br>Bachelor’s in Chemical Engineering (2002), Pune University.</p><p><strong>Professional experience</strong><br>Previously Process Design Engineer at Xytel India and Lead Process Engineer at PRAJ Industries. The profile describes experience in process design, execution, commissioning, basic engineering packages, troubleshooting and operator training; it lists work on pilot plants, reactors, catalyst testing and hydrogen-generation systems.</p></article></div></div></section></main><footer class="footer"><div class="container footer-main"><a class="brand brand-footer" href="index.html"><span class="brand-mark">T<span>.</span></span><span class="brand-name">TEXOL<small>ENGINEERING</small></span></a><p>Customized process engineering.<br>Built around your process.</p><div class="footer-links"><a href="solutions.html">Capabilities</a><a href="industries.html">Industries</a><a href="projects.html">Projects</a><a href="gallery.html">Gallery</a><a href="key-persons.html">Key Persons</a><a href="achievements.html">Achievements</a><a href="energy.html">TEXOL Energy</a><a href="contact.html">Contact</a></div></div><div class="container footer-bottom"><span>© <span class="year"></span> TEXOL Engineering.</span></div></footer><script is:inline src="/Texol_demo/script.js"></script>

